    "lem-concordance-annulus-induces-zero-surgery-cobordism": {
      "citations": [
        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "def-zero-surgery-on-a-knot",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Assume countable choice as required by the chosen tubular-neighborhood and peripheral-system data. Let K be a smooth oriented knot with compact exterior E_K, positive meridian mu_K, and preferred longitude lambda_K on the boundary torus. The zero-framed surgery manifold M(K) is the closed oriented 3-manifold obtained by gluing D²×S¹ to E_K so that the meridian boundary circle of D²×{1} is identified with lambda_K and the core {0}×S¹ is identified with mu_K. The orientation extends the orientation of E_K across the filling. Thus the filling slope is the preferred zero-linking longitude; the definition asserts no 4-manifold bounded by M(K).",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "def-locally-flat-proper-surface-and-concordance-collars",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Let $X$ be a four-dimensional manifold with boundary and let $W$ be a compact surface with boundary. An embedding $e:(W,\\partial W)\\to(X,\\partial X)$ is proper when $e^{-1}(\\partial X)=\\partial W$. It is locally flat at an interior point of $W$ when there are neighborhoods of the point and its image and a homeomorphism of pairs from those neighborhoods to $(\\mathbb R^4,\\mathbb R^2)$, with the standard linear plane $\\mathbb R^2\\subset\\mathbb R^4$. It is locally flat at a boundary point when there are such neighborhoods and a homeomorphism of pairs to $(\\mathbb R^4_+,\\mathbb R^2_+)$, where $\\mathbb R^4_+=\\{x_4\\geq0\\}$ and $\\mathbb R^2_+=\\{x_2=x_3=0,\\ x_4\\geq0\\}$; the line $\\partial\\mathbb R^2_+$ lies in $\\partial\\mathbb R^4_+$. A collar of a boundary circle of $W$ is an embedding of that circle times $[0,\\varepsilon)$ into $W$ that is the identity on the circle at parameter $0$; a concordance collar is required to agree with the corresponding product collar of the ambient end. A smooth proper surface has the analogous smooth charts and collars, which are also topological locally flat charts.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "1.2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "def-cdr-satellite-concordance-categories",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Let knots be smooth oriented knots in the standard oriented S³ and let I=[0,1]. Let C_sm be their smooth concordance classes, where equivalence is witnessed by a smooth proper annulus in S³×I. Let C_top be their locally flat topological concordance classes in that product. Let C_ex be their exotic-smooth concordance classes: equivalence is witnessed by a smooth proper annulus in a compact smooth oriented 4-manifold W together with an orientation-preserving homeomorphism of pairs (W,∂W)≅(S³×I,S³×{0,1}) matching the endpoint knots. For a nonzero integer n set R_n=Z[1/|n|]. Let C^{1/n} be the classes under equivalence witnessed by a smooth proper annulus in a compact smooth oriented 4-manifold W with boundary the two standard endpoint 3-spheres such that each boundary inclusion induces an isomorphism H_i(S³;R_n)→H_i(W;R_n) for every i. A knot is pseudo-slice if it bounds a smooth proper disk in a compact smooth 4-manifold homeomorphic to B⁴, with the boundary identified with the standard S³. A knot is Z[1/|n|]-slice if it bounds a smooth proper disk in a compact smooth 4-manifold whose boundary inclusion is an isomorphism on homology with coefficients R_n. These are sets of equivalence classes; this definition alone asserts no group structure.",
          "uses": [
            "1.2",
            "2.1"
