            "algebra"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-2-2",
          "claim": "In the exotic and topological categories, the normal-generation condition makes the capped manifold after the meridian 2-handle contractible with boundary S³. Its co-core is a smooth disk in the exotic branch and a locally flat disk in the topological branch once the resulting contractible manifold is homeomorphic to B⁴. That relative Freedman implication is the missing supplier recorded below.",
          "step": "2.2",
          "inputs": [
